db/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489335 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "84e16e8f-676c-575f-83e7-d1a743860017" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489335 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186489170 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489343 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186489298 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489343 #edb/ref 1061 653255 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489343 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "989620d9-34b2-5998-bf43-7b078a5551e7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489343 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186489388 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489345 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186489372 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489345 #edb/ref 1061 653251 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489345 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "9d911030-9a41-5eba-8339-d738949a2899" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489345 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186489385 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489372 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186489343 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489372 #edb/ref 1061 653252 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489372 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "dd795099-acd6-53fe-9be5-05e82111a5a2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489372 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186489171 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489373 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186489328 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489373 #edb/ref 1061 653257 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489373 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "e016072c-e22d-536a-a6ed-5eef7793da16" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489373 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186489386 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489385 #edb/ref 1064 "A rational number can have a decimal representation that either *ends* or *repeats*.\n\nIn this lesson, we will see how to convert rational numbers written as fractions into decimals using *long division*. \nWe begin with examples where the decimal terminates. \n\nLet's convert $\\dfrac{7}{2}$ into a decimal using long division.\n\nTo write the fraction as a decimal, we divide the numerator by the denominator:\n\n$$\n7 \\div 2\n$$\n\nWe proceed using long division as usual, stopping once we obtain a remainder of $0\\mathbin{:}$\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"150\">\n<table align=\"left\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"left\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"left\" colspan=\"2\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$\\,\\,3    {\\, . \\,} 5$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$2$</td>\n<td align=\"left\" colspan=\"2\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$\\!\\require{enclose}\\enclose{longdiv}{7   {\\, . \\,} 0}$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$-\\!\\!\\!\\!\\!\\!\\!$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$6$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$0$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$-\\!\\!\\!\\!\\!\\!\\!$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$0$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$0$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p></p></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{7}{2} = 3.5.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489385 #edb/ref 1065 15179 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489385 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "6c539020-aca7-5b8f-a2b0-b72c56336242" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489385 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489386 #edb/ref 1064 "The key takeaway for this lesson is that every repeating decimal is rational! In other words, every repeating decimal can be expressed as a ratio of two integers.\n\nFor example:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0.\\overset{―}{3} & =\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ 0.\\overset{―}{78} & =\\frac{26}{33} \\\\ 0.333\\overset{―}{67} & =\\frac{16517}{49500}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn a future lesson, we'll learn how to express a repeating decimal as a fraction. For now, you can verify these results using a calculator." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489386 #edb/ref 1065 15181 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489386 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "77b1162b-17a9-5251-8efe-31b7034274d5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489386 #edb/ref 1067 "Any Repeating Decimal is a Rational" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489387 #edb/ref 1064 "It's convenient to use the following special **bar-notation** to indicate decimals that repeat indefinitely:\n\n$$\n0.\\overline{3} = 0.333\\,333\\ldots\n$$\n\nSome decimals have two or more digits that repeat indefinitely. For example:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0.\\overset{―}{78} & =0.78\\,78\\,78\\,78… \\\\ 0.\\overset{―}{675} & =0.675\\,675\\,675…\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSome repeating decimals have non-repeating digits before the repeating part. For example:\n\n$$\n0.45\\overline{67} = 0.45\\,67\\,67\\,67\\,67\\ldots\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489387 #edb/ref 1065 15180 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489387 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "8545445f-23ee-5309-8571-5a1f6a4b253d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489387 #edb/ref 1067 "Notations for Repeating Decimals" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489388 #edb/ref 1064 "Let's consider the following rational number:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac13\n$$\n\nTo find its decimal representation, we divide $1$ by $3$ using long division, as follows:\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"150\">\n<table align=\"left\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"left\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"left\" colspan=\"4\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$\\,\\,0 \\,. 3 {\\:\\phantom{|}} 3 {\\:\\phantom{|}} 3$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$\\:\\ldots$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$3$</td>\n<td align=\"left\" colspan=\"4\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$\\!\\require{enclose}\\enclose{longdiv}{1 {\\, . \\,} 0  {\\:\\phantom{|}} 0 {\\:\\phantom{|}} 0}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$-\\!\\!\\!\\!\\!\\!\\!$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$9$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$0$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$-\\!\\!\\!\\!\\!$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$9$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$0$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$-\\!\\!\\!\\!\\!$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$9$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$\\,\\ldots$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p></p></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n\nNotice that, in this case,\n\n- the long division process never ends, and\n\n- the digit $3$ after the decimal point repeats *forever*.\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\dfrac13 = 0.333\\,333\\ldots\n$$\n\nThis is an example of a **repeating decimal** - a decimal in which the digits after the decimal point continue forever in a *repeating pattern*." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489388 #edb/ref 1065 15177 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489388 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "b877953a-1821-5fae-aebf-3ff936971679" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489388 #edb/ref 1067 "Repeating Decimals" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492222 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186492975 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492222 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186492987 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492222 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186493001 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492222 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045464 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492222 #edb/ref 1045 "Absolute Value Equations" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492222 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186492987 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492222 #edb/ref 1048 #edb/ref 17592186046648 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492222 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186048267 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492222 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "fdf293e8-c26a-525e-9d5d-8af56d0bc18f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492232 #edb/ref 1080 "$-\\frac{2}{7}$ or $2$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492232 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492232 #edb/ref 108